    "title": "Big E Doubts The New Day Vs. The Elite Will Ever Happen - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Thomas Lowson ,\n23 minutes ago\nNeither the New Day (Kofi Kingston & Xavier Woods) nor members of The Elite are in WWE right now, but Big E doubts a dream match will happen.\nFor years, fans have speculated who would triumph in such a match, but were hampered by The New Day seemingly being WWE ‘lifers.’\nThat all changed earlier this year when Kingston and Woods left WWE, reportedly after turning down a restructured extension of their contracts.\nREAD MORE: Kevin Nash Mourns 30 Years Of nWo, WWE Stars Light Up Moana Premiere, SNME Betting Odds\nREAD MORE: Sirena Linton On Possibly Joining AEW Or TNA After WWE Exit, Possible Return\nWhile speaking to Westwood One Sports Night , Big E reflected on a possible match between the two popular teams. He said,\n“I understand that there’s a lot of d*** measuring in professional wrestling. The idea of that happening now I cannot see ever happening.”\nBig E also recalled meeting The Elite years ago and how both sides gave little teases of working together, though a match never came. He said,\n“They came out in New Day shirts before. We would do little teasers. I would make little Kenny the Cleaner jokes in these little bits, but we were trying to slowly find a way to see if we could push it to just, man, imagine, especially when we were at the peak of our powers. Imagine the six of us in a ring one night only, man. I think would have been beautiful.”\nIf a match were to happen, it would have to go ahead without Big E, as he is still with WWE and has retired from action due to his neck injury.\nFollowing their exit from WWE, it was reported that The New Day were expected to eventually join AEW, though that hasn’t happened yet.",
    "summary": "Neither the New Day (Kofi Kingston & Xavier Woods) nor members of The Elite are in WWE right now, but Big E doubts a dream match will happen. The idea of that happening now I cannot see ever happening.” Big E also recalled meeting The Elite years ago and how both sides gave little teases of working together, though a match never came.",
